  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_08ab4651668e4b00b3b000a5b99d9ed5",
      "statement": "Metro rewrites `import.meta.url` in bundled dependencies to `globalThis.__ExpoImportMetaRegistry.url`; the Metro dev server populates that registry but the exported `@expo/server` runtime used in the Docker/production build does not, so any bundled dependency that runs `createRequire(import.meta.url)` — e.g. `@copilotkit/runtime`'s lazily-required adapter on the `/bff-api/agent/run` path — throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'url')` at request time and the request hangs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/server.js#L13-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cab8e34974fbd978268f9362c58b40fe704fee3d1fd4c0c962d8e0d8943409c0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_38fcace0c38a4059ab4cd9930e9085d2",
      "statement": "`frontend/mcm-app/server.js` pre-seeds `globalThis.__ExpoImportMetaRegistry = { url: pathToFileURL(__filename).href }` BEFORE `createRequestHandler` loads the exported bundle; Metro uses one shared registry whose `.url` is identical for every module, so pointing it at the server module lets `createRequire` resolve against the deployed `node_modules`. The `if (!globalThis.__ExpoImportMetaRegistry)` guard is deliberate: if a future `@expo/server` populates the registry itself, the seeding becomes a harmless no-op rather than clobbering the real value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/server.js#L13-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cab8e34974fbd978268f9362c58b40fe704fee3d1fd4c0c962d8e0d8943409c0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/server.js#L84-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3a0d5dbe67a981a7ec219aa82a5c2d7d4b3d3c1b0474b31a1c61934d97a47f07:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_066e148698d349228b3bc38b17f02c16",
      "statement": "Removing the `__ExpoImportMetaRegistry` seeding at the top of `server.js` looks like deleting dead defensive code but reintroduces a silent, production-only hang on the agent route.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/README.md#L157-L163",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8729f7af9e5e1ad730babf2773b724c87230793700b76dda5f3c2cf3905186d7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/server.js#L13-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cab8e34974fbd978268f9362c58b40fe704fee3d1fd4c0c962d8e0d8943409c0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c52fd20e842d44208c15f14a98f15cac",
      "statement": "The `createRequire(import.meta.url)` failure is thrown asynchronously inside the SSE `respond` pipeline, so the `/bff-api/agent/run` handler's own `try`/`catch` never sees it — the client observes an indefinite hang with no 500 and no error identifying the cause. That is why \"the agent route never answers, in the container only\" identifies this trap.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/agent/run%2Bapi.ts#L255-L270",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42c69011a0a4161af26b9016544de5a20cdc66d74b06e84c431cbf43f0dcb42c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://specs/012-multi-agent-mvp/HANDOFF.md#L850-L852",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f359e6203bbb900d536286951a4d82fde4adb6d2992ba0884d9b7f621419d40e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a6dd94e757b646a98140e3b296cf9901",
      "statement": "Because `@copilotkit/runtime` reaches its provider adapters through `createRequire(globalThis.__ExpoImportMetaRegistry.url)` — a bare string a static closure walk cannot see — the BFF image build runs a bundle check that re-derives every such specifier from the freshly exported `dist/server` and fails the build if one is not accounted for, converting a future production 500 on one route into a red build.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/README.md#L96-L104",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:32bf11413b212a8c6a50071659d9cdc3f869e7b8d859badc4cf576b4841b0f70:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/prune-bff-runtime-modules.mjs#L54-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:892c5fb7fac7c1162326fc4552b12b6c4ea867bda2bae7656869e6cae8d0cea2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_07c3cc4bc88c49208b3453a61eb8680c",
      "statement": "CopilotKit's React Native runtime issues its `/bff-api/agent/run` request through its own XHR-based streaming-fetch polyfill, which never passes through the axios token-refresh interceptor in `utils/token-refresh`, so an expired `mcm_access_token` cookie 401s the run with no refresh attempted. Cookie auth nonetheless works because the polyfill itself never sets `init.credentials` and instead relies on React Native's `XMLHttpRequest` default of `withCredentials = true`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/agent-fetch-refresh.ts#L1-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e1455aeef81e57035b60e915203c7f9fda2df721b60c430eb157600a8f5b34e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/token-refresh.ts#L6-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ec5bea435bf8c0d83245da7946219ab64b537499c56e8397f1dbadfe171b6df:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://specs/013-post-agent-enhancements/diagnosis-mobile-agent-no-token.md#L59-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:400199df5d5dfce44c0f4a1d9309072457317f710b9c416b018f08ff9c322ad3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_087ade58f8e748af9c66246e83e613c1",
      "statement": "`frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/agent-fetch-refresh.ts` installs a one-shot wrapper around `globalThis.fetch` that detects a 401 on the `/bff-api/agent/run` route specifically, calls `silentRefresh()`, and retries the run once with the refreshed cookie; all other requests and non-401 responses pass straight through, and a still-401 result after refresh is returned as-is rather than looping. `createRefreshingFetch` is a pure factory taking an injected `baseFetch` + `refresh` so the behavior is testable without touching any global.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/agent-fetch-refresh.ts#L55-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d574ee9be8d6c991c96390228f7b7bca7cf90ddb808244b620f027810667d91a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/unit-tests/agent-fetch-refresh.test.ts#L16-L81",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:24356cd9c8b3b6bb608a02c4919ca9cb3095eb53e1399f19da35751850b40448:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_745855899feb4affa9d68417022aa0ff",
      "statement": "Install order for the wrapper is load-bearing: it must be installed after the CopilotKit streaming-fetch polyfill but before CopilotKit issues any run, which is exactly what `assistant-polyfills.ts` / `assistant-polyfills.native.ts` are structured to guarantee as the first import of `src/app/_layout.tsx`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/_layout.tsx#L6-L9",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:332d56df92902cdfbb2e97b8f98ddc802f68e04e452551c80e155dc14b8205ae:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/assistant-polyfills.native.ts#L24-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf874aa1ba2e4699eb7cd19c8c3b115c25ac8a99708a02bf2fa788bca85b9c05:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/assistant-polyfills.ts#L18-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e2a4396bc75a9839223407818e71389a442fb0d55ba69e234bd3f08081594c0c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_143aefa2b3a848fb87fda0a84b667ea8",
      "statement": "The same wrapper implements a second, distinct recovery: a THROWN fetch error on the agent route (the dropped response stream / reset tunnel that surfaces server-side as `Cannot pipe to a closed or destroyed stream`) triggers a `RUN_RETRY_DELAY_MS` (250 ms) wait and exactly one retry. The retry is safe because a dropped connection aborts the upstream gateway turn via `@expo/server`'s `AbortController`, making the cut turn idempotent-on-failure; non-agent throws propagate unchanged, and a genuine 4xx returns a `Response` (never throws) so it is never retried.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/agent-fetch-refresh.ts#L38-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f6bfcf8ad8e455e7d581e1c1b773492e776782843c85bb3b0bc237b80f4249ab:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/agent-fetch-refresh.ts#L66-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:72dc9b74eb28cafb923a0cae1bbbe98e2658c9d34deb9fa3cdb9ece0365a6aec:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/unit-tests/agent-fetch-refresh.test.ts#L83-L137",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:17ce8d3367de34dece6b9ac43a60f601b42a720257ceb16ab2d1f29e47ae71ed:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_506f00a14f5b4a32b55a58e933706546",
      "statement": "The polyfill loader is deliberately split at the platform boundary: the default/web `assistant-polyfills.ts` installs only the refresh wrapper (the crypto/streaming globals are native on web), while `assistant-polyfills.native.ts` loads the CopilotKit crypto and streaming polyfills and then the wrapper. This exists because the polyfills' static `require`s previously placed ~596 KB of unreachable `text-encoding` / `web-streams-polyfill` code in the entry chunk for every web user.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/assistant-polyfills.native.ts#L1-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2f4db08003d84d5a590cb0e5e50ed4979fdcbefb09028bbca905085ed8878a97:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/assistant-polyfills.ts#L1-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c35b90d085747d27b1d44771802642dc3c9e1fe0ff531bf4e954cee602629d48:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e3b9fb11e4514386a8615f69a44b5bca",
      "statement": "Whether the 401 refresh-retry actually recovers a real mid-session expiry — as opposed to the failures seen under an unstable Windows/Metro harness — remained an open verification item in the source comments, and the Android E2E harness is the intended regression net for the implicit RN cookie-delivery default. The SERVER half of the chain has since been proven by the web E2E `tests/e2e/web/agent-session-refresh.spec.ts`, which drops only the access cookie, observes the `no_token` 401 the agent route sees, and shows `/bff-api/auth/refresh` rotating the cookie so the retry succeeds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/utils/agent-fetch-refresh.ts#L17-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:abc2ff3e65e6e5ad9993d59d6d5abc5e0b45fadb9e4dbc64ef43e1e3a1bb3056:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/tests/e2e/web/agent-session-refresh.spec.ts#L1-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2e14f60552703c5ada44b9311c184455b9f691cf8d50076f9a34c65434df3771:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_facd5ac2caa24ac9ac01eb2505256d42",
      "statement": "The Android mobile E2E flow `tests/e2e/mobile/agent-navigate-movie.yaml` drives the live agent stack end-to-end from the assistant dock through BFF `/run` to the gateway and back to a router push, asserting a route-independent outcome (the member ends on the named movie's detail screen) rather than which supervisor route the model chose.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/tests/e2e/mobile/agent-navigate-movie.yaml#L1-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a56d7ae9832fce123f61f93697bdb648c3677a804294029cad50a30017ff3499:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/tests/e2e/mobile/agent-navigate-movie.yaml#L39-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:064aac15276536c888760565f070054c6c94271dca4dc0b34becf406764077bd:"
        }
      ]
    }
